{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/election/Proofs.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:27:44.591657Z","id":"6515cada1d8ea52533817f02bbc27b589b104ea63cc2cbea4f650e68f9e8e4dc","body":{"detail":"The private theorem `computation` (lines 82-126) proves that the deadline is exactly `ticks + sample random % ticks`, but the public obligation Election.deadline_range only states `ticks <= next < 2*ticks`. Rewriting src/node.rs:779 as `self.config.election_ticks + 0 % self.config.election_ticks`, or fixing `sample`, would still satisfy every obligation: every node would get the same deadline, which defeats the randomized split-vote avoidance that progress (L-requirements in CORRECTNESS_PLAN.md) will need. The mutation list in jarl/tests/proof_cases/scalar_methods.rs:101-112 does not cover this case.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":135},"end":{"line":143},"content_hash":"c3a4bd293f850d10fb26ad1c472e1dbcf2af61b3fa1850cf22fcb3fc6c969909"},"suggested_fix":"Add a public obligation `deadline_exact` that exposes the SplitMix64 value from `computation`, or a seed-dependence theorem, and add a constant-sample mutation to scalar_methods.rs.","summary":"deadline_range exports only the [ticks, 2*ticks) range, so a mutation that removes the election jitter still verifies","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/election/Proofs.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:08:39.037833Z","id":"00672cb150c420436f276bc6d700bd2a5930ae638e12eec7530676f34649256d","body":{"detail":"Proofs.lean:82-126: the private theorem computation proves deadline = ticks + sample random % ticks. The public deadline_range (:135-143) states only ticks <= next < 2*ticks. election/project.json lists only elapsed_reset, deadline_range and random_advanced. A constant sample at src/node.rs:779, such as `election_ticks + 0 % election_ticks`, would still satisfy that range. scalar_methods.rs:102-112 mutates only elapsed, % to /, and deadline=0.","kind":"comment","references":"6515cada1d8ea52533817f02bbc27b589b104ea63cc2cbea4f650e68f9e8e4dc","summary":"confirmed: only the range of the deadline is exported, and no mutation removes the jitter","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/election/Proofs.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T14:31:29.696815Z","id":"c3e246ee42885878d4de9d231c7e9a58715d081c3a5c850576edc88799b0d83c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3930f70d722cec6728c49f4c2c906982bedcb057","summary":"Election.deadline_exact proves the generated deadline equals ticks + splitMix64 random % ticks, with SplitMix64 written out publicly; it is an election obligation verified in the full Jarl gate.","supersedes":"6515cada1d8ea52533817f02bbc27b589b104ea63cc2cbea4f650e68f9e8e4dc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
